From 71458294276fa2a042edc5858f4849e5182e1ad3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 04:51:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] turnip: scale the transform feedback counter offset on a6xx

vkCmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT draws too many vertices whenever
counterOffset is non-zero, failing every
dEQP-VK.transform_feedback.simple*.draw_indirect*_counter_offset_* case
on a618, a660 and a702.  The a6xx command processor holds the
CP_DRAW_AUTO counter in dwords and so shifts NUM_VERTICES_OFFSET right
by two before subtracting it, while turnip hands it a byte counter --
tu_CmdEndTransformFeedbackEXT converts one to the other -- along with a
byte stride, so only a quarter of the requested offset is taken off.

Scale the offset up by four on a6xx so that shift cancels.  a7xx shifts
the counter too and already gets a consistent pair.

Fixes: 20e12d9ef4e2 ("turnip: implement CmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/43801>

